    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "EMERGENCY\nINSTRUCTIONS\nFOR YOUR SAFETY\nJUST IN CASE...\nPAN AMERICAN\nSuper-7 Clipper Service\nCIPPER TRADE MARK PANAMFRICAN WORID AIRWAYS INC",
      "IN CASE OF ANY\nEMERGENCY LANDING\nREMEMBER THESE SAFETY RULES\nKnow the location of the emer-\ngency exit nearest you. There is\na sign that reads \"Emergency\nExit\" above each one.\n2\nKnow the location of your life\njacket—it's underneath your\nseat, or in the compartment in-\ndicated by your flight attendant.\n3\nLoosen collar and tie. Remove\nglasses and sharp objects from\npockets. Put on life jacket, if\ninstructed, and fasten seat belt.\nAdjust seat to vertical position.\nAssume proper posture to relieve\nstrain of possible sudden stop.\n5\nNever inflate your life jacket\ninside cabin. Wait until you\nget outside the plane.\nBe calm and cooperative until help comes.\nFollow the instructions of your aircraft officers.\nPRINTED IN U.S. A.\nF30-4040\n7-58-7C"
    ],
